Key Findings

1. Revised Tension definition worked perfectly – All 7 AIs correctly reported Tension: None. The definition explicitly excludes complementary differentiation (root down vs. shoot up), and every model followed it. This resolves the earlier ambiguity (5/8 saw tension in previous run).
2. Split unanimously detected – All models recognised the root/shoot asymmetry as a qualitative split. The refined definition of Split (requiring asymmetry, not simple progression) is robust.
3. No false positives on Failed Merge, Scar, or Decay – All AIs correctly returned N/A or None. This is a major improvement over the original positive control run (where most saw a failed merge and scar). The refined definitions have successfully eliminated over‑interpretation.
4. Total agreement across 7 distinct AI models – This is the highest consistency observed in any of your validation tests. It demonstrates that with well‑crafted definitions, the lens can produce reproducible, theory‑aligned outputs across a wide range of models.

